.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH powerlinux-compress 1  "PowerLinux 0.1.0" "PowerLinux Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
powerlinux\-compress \- Strip metadata and compress PNG, JPEG, WebP or MP4 files
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpowerlinux compress\fR [\fB\-\-quality\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Strip metadata and compress PNG, JPEG, WebP or MP4 files
.PP
Each FILE is written to NAME.min.EXT beside it; originals are never modified.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-quality\fR \fI<QUALITY>\fR [default: 80]
Quality from 1 (smallest) to 100 (best); ignored for PNG, which is always lossless
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIFILE\fR>
Files to compress (.png, .jpg/.jpeg, .webp, .mp4/.m4v/.mov)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH TOOLS
.PP
Compression runs these programs, which must be installed:
.TP
\fBPNG\fR
oxipng, lossless, all metadata stripped.
.TP
\fBJPEG\fR
jpegoptim, recompressed down to \-\-quality, all metadata stripped.
.TP
\fBWebP\fR
cwebp, at \-\-quality, metadata dropped.
.TP
\fBMP4\fR
ffmpeg, H.264 with a CRF derived from \-\-quality, AAC audio, metadata removed, fast\-start enabled.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Compress every PNG in a folder:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBpowerlinux compress ~/Pictures/*.png\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Shrink a video harder:
.RS 4
.nf
\fBpowerlinux compress clip.mp4 \-\-quality 50\fR
.fi
.RE
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBpowerlinux\fR(1), \fBoxipng\fR(1), \fBjpegoptim\fR(1), \fBcwebp\fR(1), \fBffmpeg\fR(1)
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
